{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/751417-are-people-born-solar","id":751417,"title":"Are people born solar?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Solar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-11-03T07:50:55-08:00","id":751417,"title":"Are people born solar?","content":"In another topic I was discussing The exalted and I went to look through the Ex3 pdf to find a description of what an exaltation is... and I can't find anything. No mention of Lytek <i>at all</i> that I can find. No discussion of an exalted shard. I did find this in the Exigent description:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ex3 pg52</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The blood of the Terrestrial Exalted spreads<br /> far across Creation, while the Celestial Exalted reincarnate<br /> endlessly.</div> </div> </div> </div>So the celestial exalted reincarnate... though that could be interpretting that each reincarnation is the same person and the power simply lies dormant in them until they need it.<br /> <br /> Then again, the Age of Exalted portion of the history shows: <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ex3 pg20</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Most of the Solars were murdered and their Essences<br /> sealed away in a jade prison\u2014for such was their power<br /> that they could reincarnate upon death.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which from my perspective is somewhat clumsy wording unless you've read 2E stuff. I could easily interpret that sentence that it was the solars themselves that could reincarnate... I hope this doesn't cause issues if someone is coming into exalted fresh on Ex3 and expects their solar to be able to be resurrected with 500GP worth of diamonds... but that's another issue.<br /> <br /> Of course then they read this and possibly get confused:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ex3 pg26</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Solars were overthrown by the Dragon-<br /> Blooded and their Exaltations imprisoned by the Sidereal<br /> Exalted, but now they have returned to try to save<br /> Creation from doom.</div> </div> </div> </div>Slightly aside:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ex3 pg25</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">While memories of past incarnations<br /> sometimes guide reincarnated Solars back into the company<br /> of their fellows from previous lives</div> </div> </div> </div>So we know that there are still memories of past lives and this is discussed many times in the charms section and even in the blurb about performance... but is it actually described <i>why</i> the solars get these past lives? Hell, from that passage on pg 20 it sounds like the solar himself is reincarnated and remember the last time he was a solar?<br /> <br /> Then I found this:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ex3 pg2</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">had done some great unrecorded deed<br /> and won Exaltation: drawn down into her body a portion<br /> of the essence of the divine Unconquered Sun.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right in the first Chapter story. So a solar exaltation is a chunk of TUS essence...<br /> <br /> and you have memories of past lives... No mention of who's past lives those are that I can find. Could be from the previous owners of the exaltation (as in previous editions), could be from your own personal past lives as a solar (this raises interesting questions about the exaltation process)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ex3 pg40</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Unconquered Sun selected his champions<br /> to reflect all aspects of his majesty</div> </div> </div> </div>From this it sounds like TUS now guides exaltations personally. Hell, from the description in the lunars write up it definitely sounds like Luna chooses her own champions:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ex3 pg46</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Chosen of the moon were forged in the chains of bondage but Luna only chooses those<br /> with the power to free themselves</div> </div> </div> </div>But then:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ex3 pg60</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Luna is the most active Incarna\u2014she<br /> still attends the Exaltation of each of<br /> her Chosen</div> </div> </div> </div>Which implies that none of the incarnae need to be there when exaltation happens, like in 2E... <br /> <br /> It can certainly be interpreted that the exaltations function as they did in 2E. Far as I can tell there's nothing gainsaying that, but if someone comes fresh into the game, how are they supposed to come to this conclusion? Unless I missed the side bar explaining what an exaltation (shard?) is.<br /> <br /> Can anybody find anything definitively explaining what an exaltation is or how it works? Or did the writers simply decide to let players come up with their explanations? Because it seems like it's written as if it works the same as it did in 2E but how the heck are you supposed to understand that from the context of these quotes? The exaltation shards aren't exactly an intuitive explanation and as far as I can tell it's still the only thing that makes sense based on how the book is written...<br /> <br /> Am I missing a chunk of exposition? A pivotal side bar that describes what the shards are? anybody?<br /> <br /> Because I'm scared that suddenly people are born as solars and the power simply lies dormant until they perform a great deed. Please find me something that says this isn't the case.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-03T07:58:40-08:00","id":751452,"title":"","content":"I wonder if the seeming contradictions are deliberate...<br /> <br /> Anyway, the answer is no. There is nothing definitively explaining Exaltation - the writers have made it clear that they're not doing that for this edition. &quot;It's a miracle!&quot; is as much of an explanation as we're going to get.<br /> <br /> As for your theory... the quotes you provided say that Exaltation is<i> awarded</i>, not embedded from birth. I believe &quot;Reincarnation&quot; in this context refers to how there are a finite number of Solar exaltations that pass from person to person, similar to (but not exactly like) how a soul gets scrubbed of its memories when someone dies and put into a new body when they are reborn.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-03T08:00:17-08:00","id":751458,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>armyofwhispers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/751417-are-people-born-solar#post751417\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because I'm scared that suddenly people are born as solars and the power simply lies dormant until they perform a great deed. Please find me something that says this isn't the case.</div> </div> </div> </div>It certainly doesn't say that they ARE born Solar, so there's that. <br /> <br /> The authors have said for years that 3e is explictly going back to the gods Choosing their Exalted, versus it being basically being little autonomous magic bullets running worthiness algorithms while scanning the entire world for their criteria to be met. <br /> <br /> Don't expect the Exaltations themselves to be described in great and exhaustive detail. That's one of the things the 3e authors and a not insignificant percentage of others (myself included) hated about 2e. If it seems confusing it's probably deliberate. Because miracles are confusing and mean different things to different people. The question &quot;is my Solar the actual reincarnation of another guy, or do I just have some of his memories somehow,&quot; is not a question that the books should answer. <br /> <br /> The Exaltations don't matter anywhere near as much to the game or to the setting as the Exalted themselves do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":3420,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","user":"Zelbinnean","date":". 11-03-2015, 11:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-03T08:00:54-08:00","id":751460,"title":"","content":"Does the idea of memory flashes from past holders of a Celestial Exaltation still exist in 3rd Edition?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-03T08:01:11-08:00","id":751462,"title":"","content":"People are born again as Solars, and while their identity isn't changed, they are also not truly separate from who they used to be. You can say Swan is nothing like Desus, but on a fundamental level, Swan is Desus, as Desus was his previous incarnation, wearing a new body and a new personality, but ultimately the same Solar. However, whether they will be a Solar or not is something determined by their actions in life, not written in their fate when they first gain a soul along with the breath of life.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;From now on, instead of saying 'half-assed', I will use 'muled'. 'This is a muled job, Chris', I will say to my friend Chris. 'You need to do better, or your ass is grass. And not, like, metaphorical grass. There are weeds growing in there as we speak.'<br /> <br /> &quot;'The DEA is after you, man' I will tell him, in all seriousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8891-khantalas","name":"Khantalas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8891_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"899"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-03T08:18:24-08:00","id":751479,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/751417-are-people-born-solar?p=751460#post751460\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does the idea of memory flashes from past holders of a Celestial Exaltation still exist in 3rd Edition?</div> </div> </div> </div>I <i>believe</i> that the devs have mentioned that that is a thing that exists, albeit in passing - something about how your Solar could enter an ancient First Age ruin and receive a sudden vision of it in its glory days. I <i>also</i> believe that they say that this was the extent of it, and that there were no intentions of making it so that you could clearly remember, well, <i>anything</i> from the First Age - it is always beyond a veil of oblivion (in the sense of forgetfulness) and dreams.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>All that I write but don't cite is simply my perspective, colored by my experiences and beliefs. I extrapolate a lot, too, so don't take it too seriously. :P","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7858-end","name":"*End","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7858_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-03T08:18:42-08:00","id":751480,"title":"","content":"I asked the devs before the book was released. The response was Exaltations are the same as they were in the past only now they aren't going to talk about the subject in the books due to issues it caused in the past.<br /> <br /> Only real change is the Incarnae now specifically chose their exalted and it isn't an automated process. Which I fully intend to ignore as it would make the Primordial War unwinnable and the Exalted all willing servants or the Primordials.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/151-hark","name":"Hark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar151_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"932"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-03T08:22:33-08:00","id":751483,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/751417-are-people-born-solar?p=751480#post751480\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I asked the devs before the book was released. The response was Exaltations are the same as they were in the past only now they aren't going to talk about the subject in the books due to issues it caused in the past.<br /> <br /> Only real change is the Incarnae now specifically chose their exalted and it isn't an automated process. Which I fully intend to ignore as it would make the Primordial War unwinnable and the Exalted all willing servants or the Primordials.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> In Ex3, we know nothing about the Primordial War, so it is possible that the gods weren't under any oaths to not directly attack the Primordials. Heck, I don't think the term &quot;Primordial&quot; is used in Ex3. <br /> <br /> Or perhaps after the war was won, Exaltations were changed so the Incarnte could choose heroes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-03T08:22:35-08:00","id":751484,"title":"","content":"No, it really wouldn't.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>SWTOR Referal: <a href=\"http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/414-gallus","name":"Gallus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"886"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-03T08:23:21-08:00","id":751485,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/751417-are-people-born-solar?p=751480#post751480\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I asked the devs before the book was released. The response was Exaltations are the same as they were in the past only now they aren't going to talk about the subject in the books due to issues it caused in the past.<br /> <br /> Only real change is the Incarnae now specifically chose their exalted and it isn't an automated process. Which I fully intend to ignore as it would make the Primordial War unwinnable and the Exalted all willing servants or the Primordials.</div> </div> </div> </div>Only if you use the 2e version of the Great Geas, but that's up to you, ultimately.<br /> <br /> I also feel like in response to the OP, I should expand on what I feel is true.<br /> <br /> In short, yes and no. I don't think that one is born an infant Solar who realizes their potential only in times of great power. Rather, you are <i>Chosen</i> by the Most High of all gods, and by imbuing you with his Essence, he makes you (in some sense) his new child, and you are reborn as a Solar, whose previous incarnations were also you, but separated by a veil of time, death, and forgetfulness. You were not born as an infant bearing their soul, but rather reborn with them as your ancient incarnations the moment the Sun let his power uplift you. At the same time, they're not you, because they had vastly different lives than you have had, and lived in a different time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>All that I write but don't cite is simply my perspective, colored by my experiences and beliefs. I extrapolate a lot, too, so don't take it too seriously. :P","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7858-end","name":"*End","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7858_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-03T08:23:43-08:00","id":751486,"title":"","content":"yeah, if you want consistency for this kind of thing, go read Heaven's Reach. its the one with all the Exaltations actually being strange digital machine stuff that evaluates whether your worthy or not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6018-raziere","name":"Raziere","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6018_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-03T08:25:25-08:00","id":751487,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/751417-are-people-born-solar?p=751480#post751480\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Only real change is the Incarnae now specifically chose their exalted and it isn't an automated process. Which I fully intend to ignore as it would make the Primordial War unwinnable and the Exalted all willing servants or the Primordials.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not necessarily. The creators of the universe need not be able to command the Incarnae except through normal social influence, only to make them unable to harm their own tribe, for the Exalted to be necessary.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;From now on, instead of saying 'half-assed', I will use 'muled'. 'This is a muled job, Chris', I will say to my friend Chris. 'You need to do better, or your ass is grass. And not, like, metaphorical grass. There are weeds growing in there as we speak.'<br /> <br /> &quot;'The DEA is after you, man' I will tell him, in all seriousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8891-khantalas","name":"Khantalas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8891_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"899"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-03T08:30:16-08:00","id":751495,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>*End</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/751417-are-people-born-solar?p=751485#post751485\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Only if you use the 2e version of the Great Geas</div> </div> </div> </div>Not even then. Not even a little bit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-03T08:30:34-08:00","id":751496,"title":"","content":"Honestly, I don't think people are born Solars because that treads too closely to the Dragonblooded's themes of inherited power. <br /> <br /> Basically, those who become Solars are people who attracted the attention of the Unconquered Sun and he saw fit to empower them. Anyone could be a hero and the Unconquered Sun grant his patronage to see those heroes reach their fullest potential.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-03T08:32:46-08:00","id":751500,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/751417-are-people-born-solar?p=751495#post751495\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not even then. Not even a little bit.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wasn't going to spend more time than I had to there - just trying to point out to people who might be confused by the claim that it's not necessarily the case. You're right, of course.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>All that I write but don't cite is simply my perspective, colored by my experiences and beliefs. I extrapolate a lot, too, so don't take it too seriously. :P","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7858-end","name":"*End","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7858_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-03T08:45:15-08:00","id":751517,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/751417-are-people-born-solar?p=751480#post751480\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I asked the devs before the book was released. The response was Exaltations are the same as they were in the past only now they aren't going to talk about the subject in the books due to issues it caused in the past.<br /> <br /> Only real change is the Incarnae now specifically chose their exalted and it isn't an automated process. Which I fully intend to ignore as it would make the Primordial War unwinnable and the Exalted all willing servants or the Primordials.</div> </div> </div> </div>Alternately, it could be a mix of the two. Perhaps the Incarna have the ability to choose a recipient, and grant them an Exaltation. However, knowing the rules of the Primordials being what they are, the Incarna explicitly designed the Exaltations such that they could not be made to <i>stop</i> Exalting people. So...in that case, the Exaltations are more or less autonomous, but the Incarna have the ability to step in and say &quot;That one.&quot; So that gives us both sides of the coin: the Incarna can actually choose their champions...if they want to. Otherwise the Exaltations will seek their own partners.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3937-guildsbounty","name":"guildsbounty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-03T09:04:06-08:00","id":751556,"title":"","content":"Here's the thing: just because the Incarnae choose someone to Exalt, it doesn't mean they do so intentionally or consciously. Just as Sun the four-armed man being staggered by a brilliant gambit of Mars in the Games of Divinity doesn't prevent him from riding the Sun on its proper course, he doesn't have to be out there, looking, every moment to choose his Exalted champions. It is a part of him now that he cannot really ignore, even if he deliberately chooses to turn his face from Creation, as Solars will continue to reincarnate. But he will also, upon meeting a Solar, or being asked about him, know he Chose them as his Exalted, and why.<br /> <br /> At least, this is my headcanon. I'm not sure how I'm gonna reconcile this with my ever-burning love for Lytek.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;From now on, instead of saying 'half-assed', I will use 'muled'. 'This is a muled job, Chris', I will say to my friend Chris. 'You need to do better, or your ass is grass. And not, like, metaphorical grass. There are weeds growing in there as we speak.'<br /> <br /> &quot;'The DEA is after you, man' I will tell him, in all seriousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8891-khantalas","name":"Khantalas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8891_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"899"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-03T09:16:57-08:00","id":751567,"title":"","content":"God <i>damn</i> am I tired of this.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>armyofwhispers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/751417-are-people-born-solar#post751417\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From this it sounds like TUS now guides exaltations personally.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The authors have said for years that 3e is explictly going back to the gods Choosing their Exalted, versus it being basically being little autonomous magic bullets running worthiness algorithms while scanning the entire world for their criteria to be met.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hark</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Only real change is the Incarnae now specifically chose their exalted and it isn't an automated process.</div> </div> </div> </div><i>The Incarnae were always choosing their Exalted.</i> Always.<br /> <br /> Especially Luna, who has always shown up personally, but even Sol! Even in previous editions! It's always been a thing!<br /> <br /> It's just that it has also been the case that they can't not choose, and that their will as choosers will continue to operate even in their absence or death. It is in fact the case that the Exaltations are personally bestowed by the hand and will of the Incarnae unto their chosen vessels, and also that they're autonomous hunter-seeker power pellets. Both those things can be true at the same time with no contradiction.<br /> <br /> And that, as near as I can tell, hasn't changed at all for 3E. In fact I don't believe that the Exaltations and how they're awarded has changed for the big five (Solars/Lunars/Sidereals/Abyssals/Dragon-Blooded) at all over the course of all three editions.<br /> <br /> Really sick and tired of people making this mistake.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-03T09:30:04-08:00","id":751581,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/751417-are-people-born-solar?p=751567#post751567\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>The Incarnae were always choosing their Exalted.</i> Always.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not a mistake. It came down word of God that Exaltations were totally automated and unable to be influenced by the Incarnae. They references in the Yu-Shan book to Incarnae choosing who gets an Exaltation were immediately called out as being written in error. I'm sure if I looked hard enough I could find a text reference in 2e concerning their automation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/151-hark","name":"Hark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar151_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"932"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-03T09:57:50-08:00","id":751606,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/751417-are-people-born-solar?p=751480#post751480\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Only real change is the Incarnae now specifically chose their exalted and it isn't an automated process. Which I fully intend to ignore as it would make the Primordial War unwinnable and the Exalted all willing servants or the Primordials.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's another problem delivered to you by (from what I've heard) Infernals. There's this Cecylene (or was it SHLIHN?) charm that makes it easier to order gods around, and it's described as a function of the Oaths the gods labour under.<br /> <br /> <i>But</i>, I'd advise going with the Ink Monkeys version of the Oaths: The Primordials were unable to give <i>any</i> metaphysically binding orders to the gods, instead ruling mostly through a combination of two things: 1) They were big and powerful enough to threaten lesser gods with destruction, and 2) All gods had an in-build list of &quot;things they're not allowed to do&quot;. Some things they weren't allowed to do included attacking a Primordial, or using [celestial bodies/the weather/lots of other things] to harm a Primordial.<br /> <br /> &quot;Empowering humans and sending them to kill primordials&quot; wasn't on the list, and the Primordials were unable to add it to said list later on.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Silencing Whisper, <i>Eclipse</i>; Amethyst, <i>Changing Moon</i>;<br /> Daughter of Charcoal and Ash, <i>Dusk</i>, and her <i>Full Moon </i>sister;<br /> Broken Crystal, <i>Infernal </i>(<i>Night</i>-, or maybe <i>Twilight</i>-equivalent).","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7262-amakawa-yuuto","name":"Amakawa Yuuto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7262_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-03T10:06:45-08:00","id":751610,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/751417-are-people-born-solar?p=751567#post751567\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">God <i>damn</i> am I tired of this.<br /> <br /> <i>The Incarnae were always choosing their Exalted.</i> Always.<br /> <br /> Especially Luna, who has always shown up personally, but even Sol! Even in previous editions! It's always been a thing!<br /> <br /> It's just that it has also been the case that they can't not choose, and that their will as choosers will continue to operate even in their absence or death. It is in fact the case that the Exaltations are personally bestowed by the hand and will of the Incarnae unto their chosen vessels, and also that they're autonomous hunter-seeker power pellets. Both those things can be true at the same time with no contradiction.<br /> <br /> And that, as near as I can tell, hasn't changed at all for 3E. In fact I don't believe that the Exaltations and how they're awarded has changed for the big five (Solars/Lunars/Sidereals/Abyssals/Dragon-Blooded) at all over the course of all three editions.<br /> <br /> Really sick and tired of people making this mistake.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm in agreement with Hark. This may be your interpretation but it's by no means the only one, nor is it the most commonly accepted as far as I can tell. Hell, in Broken Wing Crane you get a charm that severs you from the control of the primordials and the exaltation reconfigures itself for independent operation. It continues to highjack demons and force them into giving choice to people without any additional divine intervention. <br /> <br /> Exaltations can certainly operate without TUS or Luna having a direct hand in it.<br /> <br /> In <b>2E</b><br /> <br /> I'm more concerned with what we have now. <br /> <br /> If TUS is doing the exalting explicitly now, how does that jive with when he turned his gaze from the world due to solar transgression back in the first age? If he wasn't exalting new people then why did the sidereals lock away the exaltations? If he <i>was </i>involved in exalting new people, why didn't he stop when the solars pissed him off? Why not just stop adding to the problem? If the solars were so horrific that he couldn't watch, why was the jade prison even necessary?<br /> <br /> Two possible explanations that i can see: <br /> <br /> 1. The solar exaltations are outside of TUS direct control (perhaps he can steer it when he's in the mood but otherwise it's on autopilot) If this is the case then obviously Luna takes a more direct hand on the controls.<br /> <br /> 2. The solar exalted were chosen back in the primordial war and reincarnate endlessly (this isn't actually unreasonable given the mechanics of rebirth, build in a &quot;you must be this awesome to exalt&quot; bar and if they don't exalt in one life then they'll just die and try again next round. Hell this actually leaves more leeway for a # of solars that isn't pinned down at any given time) <br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> Okay I guess there is one more explanation<br /> <br /> 3. TUS is actually evil/insane and was deliberately fucking with creation by letting his toys run rampant. This would mean that the Sidereals were working directly to stop him from being able to reincarnate additional solars. Perhaps the curse didn't miss the Incarnae as much in Ex3?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-03T10:21:44-08:00","id":751626,"title":"","content":"I don't know why this thread is so long.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>armyofwhispers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/751417-are-people-born-solar#post751417\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <b>Are people born solar?</b><br /></div> </div> </div> </div>No.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-03T10:27:21-08:00","id":751675,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amakawa Yuuto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/751417-are-people-born-solar?p=751606#post751606\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's another problem delivered to you by (from what I've heard) Infernals. There's this Cecylene (or was it SHLIHN?) charm that makes it easier to order gods around, and it's described as a function of the Oaths the gods labour under.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not even close. We got that charm specifically to play off the already widely known and accepted fact that the Primordials could order around the Gods. It's actually the reason that Exaltations can't be influenced by the Incarnae, to prevent the Primordials from Ordering the Gods to Exalt only people chosen as loyal servants of the Primordials.<br /> <br /> Deathlords and Yozis having some degree of control over Abyssal and Infernal Exaltations is specifically there as a horror aspect to show the awful things that they had done to the Exaltations. Even then they can't choose who gets exalted, only withhold the Exaltation from those that they don't approve of.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/151-hark","name":"Hark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar151_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"932"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-03T10:44:54-08:00","id":751704,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/751417-are-people-born-solar?p=751581#post751581\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not a mistake. It came down word of God that Exaltations were totally automated and unable to be influenced by the Incarnae. They references in the Yu-Shan book to Incarnae choosing who gets an Exaltation were immediately called out as being written in error. I'm sure if I looked hard enough I could find a text reference in 2e concerning their automation.</div> </div> </div> </div>You got a quote on that? Because my recollection of the Word of God is the precise opposite of yours.<br /> <br /> Unless you're referring to the fact that the Incarnae can't stop Exalting people. That's been true in the past and is still true now as far as I know. But &quot;can't stop Exalting people&quot; isn't the same as &quot;totally automated and unable to be influenced by the Incarnae.&quot;<br /> <br /> The Exaltations <i>are</i> automated. They always have been. But they're automated by the will of the Incarnae. Even if you were to gut Sol like a fish, his will would continue to Exalt Solars.<br /> <br /> But he can also exercise his will to Exalt who he wants, if his eye falls upon them at an auspicious time. Those two facts aren't in contradiction.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>armyofwhispers</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hell, in Broken Wing Crane you get a charm that severs you from the control of the primordials and the exaltation reconfigures itself for independent operation. It continues to highjack demons and force them into giving choice to people without any additional divine intervention.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure how the stolen Exaltations that the Yozis have hacked in the expansion explicitly concerned with freaky awesome transhumanism has any bearing whatsoever on the Incarnae and the stock Exaltations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-03T10:49:12-08:00","id":751708,"title":"","content":"I'll admit to be being a bit confused now, if the Solars are created by Sol's whim then why weren't there any for the last Age? I'm pretty sure I saw a reference to the Jade Prison a couple times, but if the exaltation is not a free-floating entity or power then how did they &quot;imprison&quot; it without also imprisoning Sol??","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","name":"kindledRadial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1318_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-03T10:52:40-08:00","id":751710,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/751417-are-people-born-solar?p=751675#post751675\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Deathlords and Yozis having some degree of control over Abyssal and Infernal Exaltations is specifically there as a horror aspect to show the awful things that they had done to the Exaltations. Even then they can't choose who gets exalted, only withhold the Exaltation from those that they don't approve of.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's more than being able to ignore candidates. I'm pretty sure they can still steer it to candidates they want. I think it's more that they can't change the <i>awesomeness requirements</i> of exaltation. Possibly because the exaltations are still based off the solar exaltation which, I guess, simply won't attach to someone who isn't at least a certain amount awesome to start?<br /> <br /> Then again, I'm away from my abyssals and infernals books so I don't have much to back that up. Plus who knows exactly how it'll work in 3E.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-03T10:55:37-08:00","id":751714,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/751417-are-people-born-solar?p=751708#post751708\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll admit to be being a bit confused now, if the Solars are created by Sol's whim then why weren't there any for the last Age? I'm pretty sure I saw a reference to the Jade Prison a couple times, but if the exaltation is not a free-floating entity or power then how did they &quot;imprison&quot; it without also imprisoning Sol??</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably a sorcerous working.<br /> <br /> Why does it matter? It happened.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":3420,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","user":"Zelbinnean","date":". 11-03-2015, 02:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-03T10:58:20-08:00","id":751718,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/751417-are-people-born-solar?p=751704#post751704\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You got a quote on that? Because my recollection of the Word of God is the precise opposite of yours.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's like 3 or 4 forums ago. Neph was very clear about this. He build the game like a simulation, and that simulation had to include anew Exalted win-state for the Primordial War. If the Incarnae could influence the process they Primordials wouldn't have even bothered fighting, they just order the Gods to exalt Primordial loyalists.<br /> <br /> As I understand it this became a significant point of divide between him and the current team.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/151-hark","name":"Hark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar151_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"932"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-03T10:58:49-08:00","id":751719,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/751417-are-people-born-solar?p=751704#post751704\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You got a quote on that? Because my recollection of the Word of God is the precise opposite of yours.<br /> <br /> Unless you're referring to the fact that the Incarnae can't stop Exalting people. That's been true in the past and is still true now as far as I know. But &quot;can't stop Exalting people&quot; isn't the same as &quot;totally automated and unable to be influenced by the Incarnae.&quot;<br /> <br /> The Exaltations <i>are</i> automated. They always have been. But they're automated by the will of the Incarnae. Even if you were to gut Sol like a fish, his will would continue to Exalt Solars.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>What? How is that any different from saying that the exaltation process doesn't require TUS at all?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/751417-are-people-born-solar?p=751704#post751704\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure how the stolen Exaltations that the Yozis have hacked in the expansion explicitly concerned with freaky awesome transhumanism has any bearing whatsoever on the Incarnae and the stock Exaltations.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because the charm in question is worded such that all it does is cut out Yozi control. The exaltation itself does the rest. It also shows that exaltations can exist independant of divine &quot;will&quot; and I'm pretty bloody sure that's not a feature added by the <b>Yozi</b>!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-03T10:58:57-08:00","id":751720,"title":"","content":"The same reason the Sun is both a burning chariot that is also an incandescent ball of plasma traveling through the skies, and the King of Heaven. Divine concepts are rarely easily constrained by a singular nature. The Solar Exaltation can be all of the following, at the same time: the Sun's deliberate and conscious divine gift to a few select mortals, a subconscious power of his working to empower the Solars so his glory is ever-present, an automated process that works based on the Sun's innermost nature, imperishable objects made of Essence that attach themselves to your soul, memories and power colored by the Sun's Essence delivered to you in one neat package.<br /> <br /> Also, there were a number of Solars during the Second Age, continually being reborn across Creation. Even ignoring that, just because the Sun can make Exaltations doesn't mean it's trivial for him to do so.<br /> <br /> In fact, that is usually the answer to: &quot;if X can be done, why hasn't it been done a million times?&quot;. It isn't trivial to do X. Just because you can do one push up, or even ten, or hundred doesn't mean you can do a thousand, or a million.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;From now on, instead of saying 'half-assed', I will use 'muled'. 'This is a muled job, Chris', I will say to my friend Chris. 'You need to do better, or your ass is grass. And not, like, metaphorical grass. There are weeds growing in there as we speak.'<br /> <br /> &quot;'The DEA is after you, man' I will tell him, in all seriousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8891-khantalas","name":"Khantalas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8891_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"899"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-03T11:10:16-08:00","id":751765,"title":"","content":"I was going to answer the OP's question with no, but after thinking about it for a little while, I've come to a realization that the answer is no.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-03T11:12:50-08:00","id":751766,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/751417-are-people-born-solar?p=751675#post751675\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not even close. We got that charm specifically to play off the already widely known and accepted fact that the Primordials could order around the Gods. It's actually the reason that Exaltations can't be influenced by the Incarnae, to prevent the Primordials from Ordering the Gods to Exalt only people chosen as loyal servants of the Primordials.</div> </div> </div> </div>So your saying the Primordials could have just ordered the UCS to kill everyone that opposed them, but for some reason didn't?<br /> <br /> Also, automated Exaltations does not remove the issue of Primordial loyalist being Exalted. Loyalties were not one of the things checked when Exalts were choosen.<br /> <br /> Also also, what bearing does the details of the oaths from 2E have on 3E? That's a rather odd assumption to carry forward.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>SWTOR Referal: <a href=\"http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/414-gallus","name":"Gallus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"886"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-03T11:14:20-08:00","id":751771,"title":"","content":"I haven't really had time to read Ex3 in detail, but I'll admit to be confused as to why there were still a few Solars Exalting while the Unconquered Sun had his back turned from Creation. That seem to be the biggest plot hole in the Ex3 system of Exaltations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-03T11:16:55-08:00","id":751773,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/751417-are-people-born-solar?p=751771#post751771\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...but I'll admit to be confused as to why there were still a few Solars Exalting while the Unconquered Sun had his back turned from Creation.</div> </div> </div> </div>For my headcanon, which I think makes perfect sense, see basically every post I made in this thread.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;From now on, instead of saying 'half-assed', I will use 'muled'. 'This is a muled job, Chris', I will say to my friend Chris. 'You need to do better, or your ass is grass. And not, like, metaphorical grass. There are weeds growing in there as we speak.'<br /> <br /> &quot;'The DEA is after you, man' I will tell him, in all seriousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8891-khantalas","name":"Khantalas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8891_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"899"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-03T11:20:18-08:00","id":751779,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/751417-are-people-born-solar?p=751771#post751771\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I haven't really had time to read Ex3 in detail, but I'll admit to be confused as to why there were still a few Solars Exalting while the Unconquered Sun had his back turned from Creation. That seem to be the biggest plot hole in the Ex3 system of Exaltations.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Much of the power was locked away. But not all of it.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;There were a handful of Solars who survived the coup and could only watch in horror from afar as the astrological signs burned in the heavens and hundreds of glowing golden lights rose to join them before winking out, one by one.&quot;<br /> <br /> Etc. <br /> <br /> Cmon seriously someone tell me what a solid and defined answer would add to the game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-03T11:21:00-08:00","id":751781,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kirby Jerusalem</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/751417-are-people-born-solar?p=751765#post751765\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was going to answer the OP's question with no, but after thinking about it for a little while, I've come to a realization that the answer is no.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm just gonna attempt to clear this up here: Having played in 2E I know very well that exaltation is not in born in the celestial exalted. My issue is that since the writers have elected to not explain how exaltation works in the core book of Ex3 we're left with a very ambiguous system.<br /> <br /> So let me put this another way: <br /> <br /> If you were a new player of Exalted, and have never made it a practice to visit a forum on the game you play (so a basic assumption of anyone picking up a new roleplaying game), how are you supposed to come to the conclusion that solars are <b>NOT </b>reincarnated endlessly?<br /> <br /> Otherwise, could people please stop answering rhetorical questions with yes or no answers?<br /> <br /> ( not trying to call you out Kirby, you're not the only one and I'm hoping to head off others from doing the same)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-03T11:23:59-08:00","id":751814,"title":"","content":"Solars <i>are </i>reincarnated endlessly. It's just that the reincarnation doesn't happen at birth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;From now on, instead of saying 'half-assed', I will use 'muled'. 'This is a muled job, Chris', I will say to my friend Chris. 'You need to do better, or your ass is grass. And not, like, metaphorical grass. There are weeds growing in there as we speak.'<br /> <br /> &quot;'The DEA is after you, man' I will tell him, in all seriousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8891-khantalas","name":"Khantalas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8891_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"899"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-03T11:31:09-08:00","id":751856,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/751417-are-people-born-solar?p=751779#post751779\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Much of the power was locked away. But not all of it.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;There were a handful of Solars who survived the coup and could only watch in horror from afar as the astrological signs burned in the heavens and hundreds of glowing golden lights rose to join them before winking out, one by one.&quot;<br /> <br /> Etc.<br /> <br /> Cmon seriously someone tell me what a solid and defined answer would add to the game.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Cool. I haven't gotten to that part of the book yet, so I didn't read that line.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-03T11:44:21-08:00","id":751912,"title":"","content":"So... This is how I understand it.<br /> <br /> 1) Sidereal did some weird Astrology Shit to extinguish the Exaltations of the Solars they assassinated. That power went to LaLa Land, back to Unconquered Sun, no one really cares because it doesn't matter to any player character.<br /> 2) A few Solars survived so their Exaltations didn't get extinguished. These are the Solars that are running around before the Scarlet Empress vanished.<br /> 3) The Unconquered Sun is needed to create new Solar Exaltations, but since his face was turned away from Creation, he didn't notice the Solars were gone.<br /> 4) Now the UCS is back, he is personally going around Exalting people. Should that Solar die, their Exaltation does not need conscious attention from the UCS to find another worthy individual.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-03T11:47:16-08:00","id":751916,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/751417-are-people-born-solar?p=751856#post751856\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Cool. I haven't gotten to that part of the book yet, so I didn't read that line.</div> </div> </div> </div>Those aren't book quotes, they're things I made up that basically work.<br /> <br /> Though nothing in the book infers that UCS made new Solar Exaltations, just that the Solars, which had largely been gone for millennia, were returning in force.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-03T11:51:38-08:00","id":751923,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/751417-are-people-born-solar?p=751779#post751779\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Cmon seriously someone tell me what a solid and defined answer would add to the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because &quot;It's magic, just ignore it&quot; has never actually been an acceptable answer to my mind?<br /> <br /> I'd be fine with a blurb specifically calling out the fact that the exact mechanism of the exaltation is up to the storyteller. Even give a couple of possible explanations as to what's going on.<br /> <br /> This ambiguity is... displeasing<br /> <br /> Edit<br /> <br /> More accurately, I think that completely ignoring that there is a question is a mistake<br /> <br /> /Edit","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":8804,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","user":"armyofwhispers","date":". 11-03-2015, 02:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-03T11:55:58-08:00","id":751929,"title":"","content":"As far as I can tell, the Exaltations went to several places after the Usurpation. Under the Great Western Ocean, to a vault in the starry void beyond the firmament of Creation, to Unconquered Sun's closet of hidden shame. All of those things are simultaneously true for each and every Exaltation the Sidereals prevented from reincarnating.<br /> <br /> Also, each Solar is described as being part of a legacy stretching back to the beginning of the ages of man, so it's not just the Sun creating new packages of power and joy ex nihilo (though it can also be that), it's him drawing from centuries of heroic legacy and mythic acts that is by now an inherent part of the Exaltation process. I think it's actually kind of interesting, and lets me say that while Swan is Desus is the guy before Desus, Swan's legacy as a Solar is not limited to things Desus and the guy before personally experienced, witnessed or enacted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;From now on, instead of saying 'half-assed', I will use 'muled'. 'This is a muled job, Chris', I will say to my friend Chris. 'You need to do better, or your ass is grass. And not, like, metaphorical grass. There are weeds growing in there as we speak.'<br /> <br /> &quot;'The DEA is after you, man' I will tell him, in all seriousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8891-khantalas","name":"Khantalas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8891_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"899"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-03T12:02:54-08:00","id":751943,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gallus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/751417-are-people-born-solar?p=751766#post751766\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So your saying the Primordials could have just ordered the UCS to kill everyone that opposed them, but for some reason didn't?<br /> <br /> Also, automated Exaltations does not remove the issue of Primordial loyalist being Exalted. Loyalties were not one of the things checked when Exalts were choosen.<br /> <br /> Also also, what bearing does the details of the oaths from 2E have on 3E? That's a rather odd assumption to carry forward.</div> </div> </div> </div>The 2E Great Geas has always been astonishingly incoherent, because if it worked the way it actually says it works in the Core, then there's no way the Incarnae could have possibly won, because the Primordials simply order them to lose.<br /> <br /> It's not unreasonable to promulgate that vision of the Great Geas, because it is actually in the core (very early in the core in fact!) but I think it has to be self-evidently wrong. I believe it was retconned later but I'd need to get home to look at my books; my brain is telling me it was rebuilt somewhere in the Glories series.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>armyofwhispers</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you were a new player of Exalted, and have never made it a practice to visit a forum on the game you play (so a basic assumption of anyone picking up a new roleplaying game), how are you supposed to come to the conclusion that solars are <b>NOT </b>reincarnated endlessly?</div> </div> </div> </div>The constant descriptions of the Exaltation being something you receive in a moment of transcendence created in part by your own decision and force of will? Also, basic logic?<br /> <br /> Seriously. What part of Perfect Soul's exaltation makes it look like the thing was just waiting inside her from her birth until it was time to come out, as opposed to the Unconquered Sun looking down on Creation and going &quot;I like the cut of her jib. I, too, know the pain of those you depended on abandoning you. Perfect Soul, you have been Chosen.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">So... This is how I understand it.<br /> <br /> 1) Sidereal did some weird Astrology Shit to extinguish the Exaltations of the Solars they assassinated. That power went to LaLa Land, back to Unconquered Sun, no one really cares because it doesn't matter to any player character.<br /> 2) A few Solars survived so their Exaltations didn't get extinguished. These are the Solars that are running around before the Scarlet Empress vanished.<br /> 3) The Unconquered Sun is needed to create new Solar Exaltations, but since his face was turned away from Creation, he didn't notice the Solars were gone.<br /> 4) Now the UCS is back, he is personally going around Exalting people. Should that Solar die, their Exaltation does not need conscious attention from the UCS to find another worthy individual.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're overthinking this, wonder.<br /> <br /> It seems like it works just exactly the same way it did in prior editions. The Solars grew twisted and corrupt, and the Unconquered Sun turned his face from them and from Creation, but continues to Exalt them because he can't not do so. The Sidereals murdered most of the Solars and imprisoned their Exaltations (I like this term much better than Essences because Essence is sort of generic) except for a few who slipped the leash and continued to reincarnate. The Jade Prison is explicitly still a thing; it is specifically name-checked, although it appears it isn't a literal prison on the bottom of the ocean this time. The Solar Exaltations have explicitly returned out of this prison now in the Age of Sorrows, and the Unconquered Sun has turned his eyes back to Creation and is actively, rather than passively, Exalting people again. But it does not appear he is creating new Exaltations.<br /> <br /> But he was always choosing.<br /> <br /> I don't feel strongly about the Incarnae being able or unable to make new Exaltatioins, but I do feel that the mythic resonance is in favor of them not being able to; that creating the Exaltations was an act of such singular creative endeavor that it can never be accomplished again. Sol can't just hammer out a few more whenever he feels like it; that sort of feels like it cheapens them a bit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-03T12:09:42-08:00","id":751960,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/751417-are-people-born-solar?p=751943#post751943\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're overthinking this, wonder.<br /> <br /> It seems like it works just exactly the same way it did in prior editions. The Solars grew twisted and corrupt, and the Unconquered Sun turned his face from them and from Creation, but continues to Exalt them because he can't not do so. The Sidereals murdered most of the Solars and imprisoned their Exaltations (I like this term much better than Essences because Essence is sort of generic) except for a few who slipped the leash and continued to reincarnate. The Jade Prison is explicitly still a thing; it is specifically name-checked, although it appears it isn't a literal prison on the bottom of the ocean this time. The Solar Exaltations have explicitly returned out of this prison now in the Age of Sorrows, and the Unconquered Sun has turned his eyes back to Creation and is actively, rather than passively, Exalting people again. But it does not appear he is creating new Exaltations.<br /> <br /> But he was always choosing.<br /> <br /> I don't feel strongly about the Incarnae being able or unable to make new Exaltatioins, but I do feel that the mythic resonance is in favor of them not being able to; that creating the Exaltations was an act of such singular creative endeavor that it can never be accomplished again. Sol can't just hammer out a few more whenever he feels like it; that sort of feels like it cheapens them a bit.</div> </div> </div> </div>This makes sense. Especailly the overthinking part. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> One day, I'll actually sit down and read the whole Ex3 instead of just relying on what I read on the forums while running Queries at work. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-03T12:12:23-08:00","id":751980,"title":"","content":"The Second Edition corebook does outright say that Exaltation had to be independent from the gods because otherwise the Primordials could just order them to reabsorb the Essence. Even within its own logic, how this squares against Primordials who never ordered the gods to never rebel to the slightest degree ever, or to turn their power upon the Exalted, I do not know. In Third Edition, it's not an issue, since we never even introduce the premise that the Primordials can give absolute commands to the gods, sp that's all cleared up. Nephilpal may have come up with a whole idea about how you absolutely need to address a win condition for the Primordial War and introduce the premise that the Primordials could give the gods absolute orders but, not to put too fine a point of that, that was Nephilpal being Nephilpal. As for the original question, I would say one should read page 35 of the book again, as I think that addresses the issues (the significance of Luna is that she not only Chooses her Exalted, she actually personally turns up to you when she does so; like, she literally, physically appears right in front of you to welcome you to being Exalted. She might even do some things alongside you for a little while, or carry you away for a whimsical adventure, although that's an extreme outlier even for Lunars).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-03T12:21:47-08:00","id":751989,"title":"","content":"Luna's an awesome patron/matron/patroness/what-have-you. I mean, perhaps <i>being</i> Lunar isn't really fun, but Luna is definitely the least distant of the Incarnae to her Chosen. Well, insofar as least distant means &quot;attends all of their Exaltations.&quot; It's still on the level of only ever <i>seeing</i> her once, most likely, but the point stands that <i>all</i> Lunars have met Luna, at the time of their becoming Chosen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>All that I write but don't cite is simply my perspective, colored by my experiences and beliefs. I extrapolate a lot, too, so don't take it too seriously. :P","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7858-end","name":"*End","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7858_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-03T13:20:02-08:00","id":752148,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>armyofwhispers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/751417-are-people-born-solar?p=751923#post751923\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because &quot;It's magic, just ignore it&quot; has never actually been an acceptable answer to my mind?<br /> <br /> I'd be fine with a blurb specifically calling out the fact that the exact mechanism of the exaltation is up to the storyteller. Even give a couple of possible explanations as to what's going on.<br /> <br /> This ambiguity is... displeasing</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah it is definitely worth wasting wordcount on a sidebar that says &quot;do what you want.&quot; Totally.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-03T13:46:32-08:00","id":752186,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/751417-are-people-born-solar?p=751771#post751771\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I haven't really had time to read Ex3 in detail, but I'll admit to be confused as to why there were still a few Solars Exalting while the Unconquered Sun had his back turned from Creation. That seem to be the biggest plot hole in the Ex3 system of Exaltations.</div> </div> </div> </div>I suspect that Sol can turn away from Creation in the sense that he limits his interaction with it, but given that he's a fundamental force of Creation, there's no way for him to cut ties completely.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>*End</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/751417-are-people-born-solar?p=751989#post751989\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Luna's an awesome patron/matron/patroness/what-have-you. I mean, perhaps <i>being</i> Lunar isn't really fun, but Luna is definitely the least distant of the Incarnae to her Chosen. Well, insofar as least distant means &quot;attends all of their Exaltations.&quot; It's still on the level of only ever <i>seeing</i> her once, most likely, but the point stands that <i>all</i> Lunars have met Luna, at the time of their becoming Chosen.</div> </div> </div> </div>Luna is the best.<br /> <br /> Being a Lunar is probably a sweet deal for Lunars. It's a suite of awesome powers and the only mandate seems to be 'follow your instincts and your passions.' Lunar society works hard to rescue those born in Imperial controlled areas, which is more than a newly-born Solar gets, but otherwise leaves people to their own devices, which is something Sidereals and Dragon-Blooded can't hope for.<br /> <br /> Yes, if your deepest desire was to spend the rest of your life in a little Imperial town, making pottery with your family, Exalted as a Lunar would suck. However, I'm not sure that sort of person would get a Lunar Exaltation anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":296,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","user":"hippokrene","date":". 11-03-2015, 04:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-03T14:04:40-08:00","id":752215,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/751417-are-people-born-solar?p=752186#post752186\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Luna is the best.<br /> <br /> Being a Lunar is probably a sweet deal for Lunars. It's a suite of awesome powers and the only mandate seems to be 'follow your instincts and your passions.' Lunar society works hard to rescue those born in Imperial controlled areas, which is more than a newly-born Solar gets, but otherwise leaves people to their own devices, which is something Sidereals and Dragon-Blooded can't hope for.<br /> <br /> Yes, if your deepest desire was to spend the rest of your life in a little Imperial town, making pottery with your family, Exalted as a Lunar would suck. However, I'm not sure that sort of person would get a Lunar Exaltation anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>I suppose I was thinking more in the terms of &quot;immense inner turmoil&quot; that seems to be a thing from what few hints I've seen, when referring to the whole &quot;not necessarily fun&quot; thing. That said, you're right in many ways... but then, as a Lunar, maybe you're suddenly wondering, as you lead your armies against the Realm/do whatever... are you really the monster they said you were?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>All that I write but don't cite is simply my perspective, colored by my experiences and beliefs. I extrapolate a lot, too, so don't take it too seriously. :P","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7858-end","name":"*End","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7858_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-03T14:15:11-08:00","id":752231,"title":"","content":"Being Solar can't be an aspect of birth. The main problem being that the ages are all wrong. People suddenly started Exalting Solar this year, across all age groups and demographics. So unless there has been a trickle of Solar exaltations going on for the last thirty years or so, and Exaltation occurs at a random age (it does), AND they all just happened to occur THIS year, then that's impossible.<br /> <br /> Fun thought exercise though. &quot;What do we really know, REALLY?&quot; is a fun question to ask of 3e. Everything is so shiny and new yay.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Don't feel bad. People tell the developers they get Exalted wrong all the time. -hippokrene","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4729-childofthesun1","name":"Childofthesun1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4729_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"853"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-03T14:23:24-08:00","id":752242,"title":"","content":"I'd say that if a Lunar can find something personal that they can focus that rage into accomplishing, they're sitting pretty. I mean, on a long enough timespan, it might eventually become an issue that you join the Silver Pact to alleviate but really, who can hope to be consistently at ease for centuries?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-03T14:33:54-08:00","id":752254,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Childofthesun1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/751417-are-people-born-solar?p=752231#post752231\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Being Solar can't be an aspect of birth. The main problem being that the ages are all wrong. People suddenly started Exalting Solar this year, across all age groups and demographics. So unless there has been a trickle of Solar exaltations going on for the last thirty years or so, and Exaltation occurs at a random age (it does), AND they all just happened to occur THIS year, then that's impossible.<br /> <br /> Fun thought exercise though. &quot;What do we really know, REALLY?&quot; is a fun question to ask of 3e. Everything is so shiny and new yay.</div> </div> </div> </div>Holy crap!<br /> <br /> Good catch! This actually makes sense based on the Ex3 manual. <br /> <br /> This is exactly what I was looking for!<br /> <br /> Thanks!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-03T17:07:58-08:00","id":752474,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>armyofwhispers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/751417-are-people-born-solar?p=752254#post752254\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Holy crap!<br /> <br /> Good catch! This actually makes sense based on the Ex3 manual.<br /> <br /> This is exactly what I was looking for!<br /> <br /> Thanks!</div> </div> </div> </div>You're welcome! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Don't feel bad. People tell the developers they get Exalted wrong all the time. -hippokrene","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4729-childofthesun1","name":"Childofthesun1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4729_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"853"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-03T19:44:57-08:00","id":752853,"title":"","content":"It's a good point about the vast majority of solar exaltations all coming back at once. Though I'm curious now whether this is because the exaltations (the items) were broken out of the Jade Prison or because Sol has decided to turn back to Creation and bestow exaltation (an action he and only he can do) upon worthy people all at once. In 2E it was obvious that the former was canon, but now I'm wondering if the latter might be a valid canon as well? Makes me wonder what would cause Sol to suddenly want to give the Solars another shot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","name":"kindledRadial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1318_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-03T19:58:31-08:00","id":752861,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/751417-are-people-born-solar?p=752853#post752853\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's a good point about the vast majority of solar exaltations all coming back at once. Though I'm curious now whether this is because the exaltations (the items) were broken out of the Jade Prison or because Sol has decided to turn back to Creation and bestow exaltation (an action he and only he can do) upon worthy people all at once. In 2E it was obvious that the former was canon, but now I'm wondering if the latter might be a valid canon as well? Makes me wonder what would cause Sol to suddenly want to give the Solars another shot.</div> </div> </div> </div>My guess is, he's giving the Solars another shot because he just had his door kicked down by 150 shards demanding reincarnation instructions all at once. They trickle in, the first he tells to shoo and figure it out itself. The second he thinks &quot;Well, that hasn't happened for a century. Eh.&quot; And he shoos that one off too. The third shows up and he thinks that's never happened before, and before he can shoo it away three more show up. Then within the next five minutes he's got over a hundred shards bouncing up and down before him. That'd shake you out of any trance pretty well.<br /> <br /> So he Exalts nearly 140 Solars personally over the next few days. Sol's face is turned firmly back to Creation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Don't feel bad. People tell the developers they get Exalted wrong all the time. -hippokrene","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4729-childofthesun1","name":"Childofthesun1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4729_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"853"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-03T20:18:34-08:00","id":752874,"title":"","content":"Anathema activists have long claimed that people are 'born Solar.' There's no reliable evidence that this is the case. Rather, most Immaculate experts agree that anathemahood is a complex condition that often involves DEMONIC POSSESSION, rising above one's station, engaging in acts of destruction and violence, and TERRORISM against the Realm.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-03T20:35:48-08:00","id":752888,"title":"","content":"I'll admit, of all the morality issues involving Exaltation, a civil rights struggle is the last I thought would pop up. But you did it. You managed to surprise me when I thought Exalted could no longer do that.<br /> <br /> Congratulations. Here, have a beast of resplendent liquid.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;From now on, instead of saying 'half-assed', I will use 'muled'. 'This is a muled job, Chris', I will say to my friend Chris. 'You need to do better, or your ass is grass. And not, like, metaphorical grass. There are weeds growing in there as we speak.'<br /> <br /> &quot;'The DEA is after you, man' I will tell him, in all seriousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8891-khantalas","name":"Khantalas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8891_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"899"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-03T20:38:36-08:00","id":752890,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/751417-are-people-born-solar?p=752874#post752874\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anathema activists have long claimed that people are 'born Solar.' There's no reliable evidence that this is the case. Rather, most Immaculate experts agree that anathemahood is a complex condition that often involves DEMONIC POSSESSION, rising above one's station, engaging in acts of destruction and violence, and TERRORISM against the Realm.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I'm beautiful in my way,<br /> 'cause the UCS makes no mistakes,<br /> I'm on the righteous track, baby,<br /> I was born this way, born this way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","name":"kindledRadial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1318_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-03T20:46:20-08:00","id":752899,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>*End</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/751417-are-people-born-solar?p=751989#post751989\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Luna's an awesome patron/matron/patroness/what-have-you. I mean, perhaps <i>being</i> Lunar isn't really fun, but Luna is definitely the least distant of the Incarnae to her Chosen. Well, insofar as least distant means &quot;attends all of their Exaltations.&quot; It's still on the level of only ever <i>seeing</i> her once, most likely, but the point stands that <i>all</i> Lunars have met Luna, at the time of their becoming Chosen.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh pfft, that's nothing. All of MY Chosen have also met me once.<br /> <br /> I'm usually disguised as an angry hobo who steals things from them! That's why they don't know! But that doesn't mean I don't care.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/789-mercury","name":"Mercury","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar789_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-03T20:48:21-08:00","id":752902,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>*End</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/751417-are-people-born-solar?p=751479#post751479\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I <i>believe</i> that the devs have mentioned that that is a thing that exists, albeit in passing - something about how your Solar could enter an ancient First Age ruin and receive a sudden vision of it in its glory days. I <i>also</i> believe that they say that this was the extent of it, and that there were no intentions of making it so that you could clearly remember, well, <i>anything</i> from the First Age - it is always beyond a veil of oblivion (in the sense of forgetfulness) and dreams.</div> </div> </div> </div>One of the fictions for the skills is a solar playing music and saying words that were remembered from a past life as Shining Bhodisattva.<br /> <br /> Your Hun and Po aren't past lives as a Solar, but your Solar Essence is the past self.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-03T20:51:09-08:00","id":752930,"title":"","content":"Strangely, I don't think the core book uses the words Hun and Po, or even says anything about people having two connected but separate souls. It might very well be that hungry ghosts and other, more sapient abominations against Creation ultimately arise from the tattered remains of a single soul.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;From now on, instead of saying 'half-assed', I will use 'muled'. 'This is a muled job, Chris', I will say to my friend Chris. 'You need to do better, or your ass is grass. And not, like, metaphorical grass. There are weeds growing in there as we speak.'<br /> <br /> &quot;'The DEA is after you, man' I will tell him, in all seriousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8891-khantalas","name":"Khantalas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8891_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"899"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-03T21:04:20-08:00","id":752964,"title":"","content":"One piece of fiction mentions a po. The text mentions upper and lower soul elements, and hungry ghosts coming from the lower.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Planned Exalted Campaign: <a href=\"http://worldunbent.com\" target=\"_blank\">Legends of a World Unbent</a> - also hosts my Minecraft servers. : )","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2860-vekseid","name":"Vekseid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2860_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-03T21:07:48-08:00","id":752978,"title":"","content":"I admit, it is my fault for not reading any fiction in an Onyx Path or White Wolf book that doesn't involve changelings or Perfect Soul, so I completely missed that. But without that, the upper and lower soul do not need to be separate, distinct entities while alive, just like your legs and head are (usually) not separate from your torso.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;From now on, instead of saying 'half-assed', I will use 'muled'. 'This is a muled job, Chris', I will say to my friend Chris. 'You need to do better, or your ass is grass. And not, like, metaphorical grass. There are weeds growing in there as we speak.'<br /> <br /> &quot;'The DEA is after you, man' I will tell him, in all seriousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8891-khantalas","name":"Khantalas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8891_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"899"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-03T21:24:38-08:00","id":752995,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/751417-are-people-born-solar?p=751480#post751480\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Only real change is the Incarnae now specifically chose their exalted and it isn't an automated process. Which I fully intend to ignore as it would make the Primordial War unwinnable and the Exalted all willing servants or the Primordials.</div> </div> </div> </div>Only if the Primordials had the power to order the Incarnae to do anything they wanted - which was a silly idea. The Geas prevented the Incarnae from personally attacking the Primordials. That's it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 11-04-2015, 12:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-03T21:30:19-08:00","id":753001,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/751417-are-people-born-solar?p=751581#post751581\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not a mistake. It came down word of God that Exaltations were totally automated and unable to be influenced by the Incarnae. They references in the Yu-Shan book to Incarnae choosing who gets an Exaltation were immediately called out as being written in error. I'm sure if I looked hard enough I could find a text reference in 2e concerning their automation.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yes they were. But there's no need to repeat that in 3E. Exaltations as &quot;things&quot; is something that's being aggressively downplayed (though not removed entirely). What the writers said earlier discussing the Solar Exaltations that occurred while the Unconquered Sun had his back turned to Creation was that his decrees are so powerful not even he can stop it, so Exaltation does continue without him, but its still his will and judgment that drives it.... it just does so no matter how he feels about it later.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-03T21:33:55-08:00","id":753004,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/751417-are-people-born-solar?p=751912#post751912\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So... This is how I understand it.<br /> <br /> 1) Sidereal did some weird Astrology Shit to extinguish the Exaltations of the Solars they assassinated. That power went to LaLa Land, back to Unconquered Sun, no one really cares because it doesn't matter to any player character.<br /> 2) A few Solars survived so their Exaltations didn't get extinguished. These are the Solars that are running around before the Scarlet Empress vanished.<br /> 3) The Unconquered Sun is needed to create new Solar Exaltations, but since his face was turned away from Creation, he didn't notice the Solars were gone.<br /> 4) Now the UCS is back, he is personally going around Exalting people. Should that Solar die, their Exaltation does not need conscious attention from the UCS to find another worthy individual.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I don't think so - because that removes the direct connection between the PCs and the fallen heroes of the First Age. There are multiple references to the power of the Solar Exalted being SEALED AWAY - not destroyed. Now where that was accomplished, I don't know.<br /> <br /> The Unconquered Sun is back to taking a more active part in Exaltation, but that doesn't mean he's creating more Exaltations.... to the extent Exaltations are a &quot;thing&quot; at all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-03T21:42:59-08:00","id":753019,"title":"","content":"He was always active in Exaltation. As long as there is even a single Zenith being reborn across all of Creation, the Sun, Holiest of Holies, King of Heaven, Shining Guardian of the Universe and Bastion of Virtue, will take the time of day to take measure of his newly Chosen priest, and compose a message specifically intended for and addressed to that one Solar. He might not be as involved with the other Castes (in fact, I'm not sure the other Castes are even allowed to receive direct messages from the Sun, like Moray Darktide did in 2nd Edition), but throughout the Second Age, he's always known of who are Exalted, and he has at the very least implicitly given his approval to all the heroes that act with the Blessing of the Sun.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;From now on, instead of saying 'half-assed', I will use 'muled'. 'This is a muled job, Chris', I will say to my friend Chris. 'You need to do better, or your ass is grass. And not, like, metaphorical grass. There are weeds growing in there as we speak.'<br /> <br /> &quot;'The DEA is after you, man' I will tell him, in all seriousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8891-khantalas","name":"Khantalas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8891_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"899"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-03T22:01:57-08:00","id":753033,"title":"","content":"I thought there were more then 150 Solar Exaltations now, not counting possible Abyssals and such? Granted, the book doesn't actually say hard numbers other then that Sideral's are still limited to 100.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9034-bulshock","name":"Bulshock","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-03T22:08:39-08:00","id":753042,"title":"","content":"Is there even anything in 3rd Edition canon saying that Abyssals are &quot;inverted&quot; Solars, or that there is even a direct link between the two Exaltations other than the superficial similarities? Because I really liked the idea of an Abyssal knowing that they could shed what they've become - especially those who knew, and didn't even consider pursuing it, but with the 3rd Edition's focus on &quot;romance of the dead&quot; and &quot;chivalry&quot;, Abyssals appear to be moving away from being struggling anti-heroes (in the classic sense, not the modern sense) with a very real punishment looming over them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;From now on, instead of saying 'half-assed', I will use 'muled'. 'This is a muled job, Chris', I will say to my friend Chris. 'You need to do better, or your ass is grass. And not, like, metaphorical grass. There are weeds growing in there as we speak.'<br /> <br /> &quot;'The DEA is after you, man' I will tell him, in all seriousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8891-khantalas","name":"Khantalas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8891_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"899"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-03T22:15:43-08:00","id":753046,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khantalas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/751417-are-people-born-solar?p=753042#post753042\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there even anything in 3rd Edition canon saying that Abyssals are &quot;inverted&quot; Solars, or that there is even a direct link between the two Exaltations other than the superficial similarities?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Nothing more than existed in the First Edition corebook, which is to say it's still really obvious without it being said.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-04T00:37:28-08:00","id":753270,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khantalas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/751417-are-people-born-solar?p=752888#post752888\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll admit, of all the morality issues involving Exaltation, a civil rights struggle is the last I thought would pop up. But you did it. You managed to surprise me when I thought Exalted could no longer do that.<br /> <br /> Congratulations. Here, have a beast of resplendent liquid.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well that's basically what it is. The Immaculate religion teaches everyone that Solars are evil monsters, and the Solars are going &quot;Hey guys, we're people too! Honest!&quot; This came up for me just a few weeks ago, in the Second Breath quest thread. We're trying to convince some Immaculate Wyld Hunt guys not to kill us. It's pretty much impossible to fight logically, so you use the same tactics used in the Civil Rights movement. Suffer until they realize you're people and they stop. It's had...mixed results, historically.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Don't feel bad. People tell the developers they get Exalted wrong all the time. -hippokrene","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4729-childofthesun1","name":"Childofthesun1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4729_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"853"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-04T00:50:03-08:00","id":753289,"title":"","content":"&quot;Are Terrestrials even people, bro.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;From now on, instead of saying 'half-assed', I will use 'muled'. 'This is a muled job, Chris', I will say to my friend Chris. 'You need to do better, or your ass is grass. And not, like, metaphorical grass. There are weeds growing in there as we speak.'<br /> <br /> &quot;'The DEA is after you, man' I will tell him, in all seriousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8891-khantalas","name":"Khantalas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8891_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"899"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-04T07:21:18-08:00","id":753956,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bulshock</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/751417-are-people-born-solar?p=753033#post753033\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought there were more then 150 Solar Exaltations now, not counting possible Abyssals and such? Granted, the book doesn't actually say hard numbers other then that Sideral's are still limited to 100.</div> </div> </div> </div>The devs have said that exact numbers of Exaltations are pretty much out the window, like in the original release of EX1. There are &quot;around 300 Solars&quot; and &quot;perhaps 400 or 500 Lunars,&quot; as I recall.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />&quot;The true object of all human life is play. Earth is a task garden; heaven is a playground.&quot; -G.K. Chesterton","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/53-blackwingedheaven","name":"blackwingedheaven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar53_3.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-04T09:06:37-08:00","id":754114,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/751417-are-people-born-solar?p=752902#post752902\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of the fictions for the skills is a solar playing music and saying words that were remembered from a past life as Shining Bhodisattva.<br /> <br /> Your Hun and Po aren't past lives as a Solar, but your Solar Essence is the past self.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is honestly one of the big reasons I started this thread. The new core goes on about reincarnation and past lives and stuff but the writers deliberately avoid talking about the concept of the solar exaltation bonding itself to your soul and passing along those memories from past holders of the exaltation.<br /> <br /> Are new players supposed to somehow intuit that the exaltation is a third soul that gives you memories? There aren't even that many mentions of the exaltation as a separate thing from Sol or the Solars. There's a lot of talk about how the new exalt feels a rush of power in but the explanation is only really clear if you've played in 2E.<br /> <br /> Y'know what I think of when I hear talk about amazing power, reincarnations and past memories? Avatar the last airbender.<br /> <br /> That dude got exalted 10,000 years ago and it's been following him through his lives ever since.. <br /> <br /> Admittedly he has immediate access to his full power even if he doesn't know how to use it but I could definitely forgive someone for assuming that exaltation was similar. Especially since<i> there is no alternate explanation offered!</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-04T09:10:48-08:00","id":754145,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khantalas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/751417-are-people-born-solar?p=753042#post753042\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there even anything in 3rd Edition canon saying that Abyssals are &quot;inverted&quot; Solars, or that there is even a direct link between the two Exaltations other than the superficial similarities? Because I really liked the idea of an Abyssal knowing that they could shed what they've become - especially those who knew, and didn't even consider pursuing it, but with the 3rd Edition's focus on &quot;romance of the dead&quot; and &quot;chivalry&quot;, Abyssals appear to be moving away from being struggling anti-heroes (in the classic sense, not the modern sense) with a very real punishment looming over them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is there anything in the core book of 2E even? Seems like the kind of thing the hold onto until the actual splat book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-04T09:19:32-08:00","id":754157,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>armyofwhispers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/751417-are-people-born-solar?p=754114#post754114\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Are new players supposed to somehow intuit that the exaltation is a third soul that gives you memories?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think they're given all the information that is necessary for understanding how to play the Exalted, and they can fill out the remaining details themselves if they're actually interested.<br /> <br /> People are evidently not born as Solar Exalted, since it states that it comes upon one under certain circumstances. Will some people interpret this in terms of &quot;Exaltation comes upon people who were already Solars in a past life&quot;? Why not?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-04T09:50:55-08:00","id":754288,"title":"","content":"I fail to see how further or more detailed explanation is required for the play experience to make sense.<br /> <br /> It sounds like some amount of baggage is being carried over and it's not the book's job to constantly say &quot;forget all the stuff that the last edition told you was true.&quot;<br /> <br /> That may not be a satisfying answer but 3e in no way requires you to understand how the setting worked in 2e for it to make sense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-04T10:37:41-08:00","id":754419,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khantalas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/751417-are-people-born-solar?p=753042#post753042\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there even anything in 3rd Edition canon saying that Abyssals are &quot;inverted&quot; Solars, or that there is even a direct link between the two Exaltations other than the superficial similarities? Because I really liked the idea of an Abyssal knowing that they could shed what they've become - especially those who knew, and didn't even consider pursuing it, but with the 3rd Edition's focus on &quot;romance of the dead&quot; and &quot;chivalry&quot;, Abyssals appear to be moving away from being struggling anti-heroes (in the classic sense, not the modern sense) with a very real punishment looming over them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually REALLY hope they go a different route this edition. At the very least I know that the devs have admitted that the constant use of &quot;mirror&quot; charms and of inverted solar themes was widely perceived as boring, and I think that sentiment was mostly echoed here by the player base. If Abyssals are still made from Solar exaltations in Ex3 then i sincerely hope that this transformation is more unique than simply taking a working Solar exaltation and covering it with enough black lipstick and goth glitter to make it seem spooky. Perhaps instead of using the exaltations (as an item) stolen from the Jade Prison the Death Lords used the ghosts of powerful first age solars as components, creating new lineages of dark heroism?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","name":"kindledRadial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1318_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-04T10:41:00-08:00","id":754425,"title":"","content":"Hey, Solars are certainly more goth than Abyssals. And most Abyssals don't even wear lipstick - their lips are naturally like that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;From now on, instead of saying 'half-assed', I will use 'muled'. 'This is a muled job, Chris', I will say to my friend Chris. 'You need to do better, or your ass is grass. And not, like, metaphorical grass. There are weeds growing in there as we speak.'<br /> <br /> &quot;'The DEA is after you, man' I will tell him, in all seriousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8891-khantalas","name":"Khantalas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8891_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"899"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-04T11:06:52-08:00","id":754551,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/751417-are-people-born-solar?p=754288#post754288\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I fail to see how further or more detailed explanation is required for the play experience to make sense.<br /> <br /> It sounds like some amount of baggage is being carried over and it's not the book's job to constantly say &quot;forget all the stuff that the last edition told you was true.&quot;<br /> <br /> That may not be a satisfying answer but 3e in no way requires you to understand how the setting worked in 2e for it to make sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm talking about how exaltion in 3E is written as if things that were true in 2E are still true. Except they aren't explained in 3E. I think we can all agree that exaltation is pretty pivotal to the setting. <br /> <br /> It's more like the writers require us to carry all the baggage through from 2E. Otherwise it doesn't make a whole lot of sense. <br /> <br /> I'm not saying that an explanation of exaltation is necessary to play Exalted. It's really not. Most often it happens off screen. It's a big part of most pre-game history...<br /> <br /> Then again so is the Scarlet Empress disappearing. It's a big event that happened in the past. It's important only to set the scene. Hell, it's less important to the characters for the game. It would be less likely to run through an exact play by play of how her redness actually went poof... and yet we have half a page giving out story ideas of the possibilities. They give examples of what could be going on that you can use as read <u><b>or build upon!</b></u> They give people ideas that spark creativity. They don't pin it down to one answer but they also don't cast it adrift. <br /> <br /> You've mentioned that you consider a side bar on the exaltations themselves a 'waste of word count.' I say that the exaltations are bloody well important enough that they can give a few ideas of what could be going on. Given a range of possibilities ensures that people actually think about the answer and possibly come up with something cool on their own. <br /> <br /> Writing a simple sidebar would do three things:<br /> <br /> 1. Provide a simple explanation for people wondering &quot;what is this exaltation thing and how does it work&quot; <br /> <br /> 2. It allows people to build upon what's already there to create cool ways to explain what's going on. Not everybody is/wants to be creative enough to fill in these kind of blanks in a setting on their own.<br /> <br /> 3. It creates a sense of internal setting consistency that doesn't rely on &quot;it's f***ing magic&quot;<br /> <br /> I ask you one question:<br /> <br /> Why is it the player/storytellers job to fill in blanks in a setting<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-04T11:14:21-08:00","id":754574,"title":"","content":"Here's the thing though: the CHARACTERS don't know how true soul-metaphysics works. So is it something that needs to be laid out in the Core? What is harmed by the whole thing being ambiguous and mysterious?<br /> <br /> you don't need to spell everything out to have a sense of consistency. You can leave things working in a way that creates a sense of a vaster picture that doesn't lay all the pieces out as definable up front. Because in a mythic setting, you want a sense of &quot;magic&quot;. Second edition ran into the problem where the setting metaphysics were so laid out it actually made the setting feel smaller than reality and artificial rather than vast and full of wonders. And worse, it made Exaltations feel like the real power rather than the character.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying the goal is &quot;throw a lot of nonsense at a wall and see what sticks&quot;, but holding things back and treating them as undefinable can serve the setting themes. Don't think &quot;Lost&quot; (where there was just nonsense, no writer plan), rather think &quot;Sandman&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 11-04-2015, 02:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-04T11:24:16-08:00","id":754587,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>armyofwhispers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/751417-are-people-born-solar?p=754551#post754551\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why is it the player/storytellers job to fill in blanks in a setting?</div> </div> </div> </div>What value does a single Word of God answer provide? What does it do except end OOC or IC debate that might happen at tables before it even could start, since someone can point at a book and say &quot;page N says it means X and it works in Y way so you're wrong?&quot;<br /> <br /> I am sure people who never played Exalted til 3e will not feel like they need to pull from 2e for the setting to feel satisfactory. Again if you feel the need to do so that's frankly your hangup to deal with. The fact that YOU find it to be a problem doesn't mean that there is an objective problem there. <br /> <br /> How are the Exaltations more important than the Exalted? What value does answering the question &quot;what is (an) Exaltation&quot; in an OOC context actually provide? How does it actually facilitate gaming in the system or the setting? <br /> <br /> The fact that the Empress disappeared is much more important to the setting than a philosophical/physics discussion of &quot;what is an Exaltation.&quot; The Empress had to be gone for the story of the Solars' return to be possible since they can't effectively stand against a unified, powerful Realm. The question of &quot;what exactly is this power?&quot; Might be interesting, but answering it isn't necessary for games to be played in the setting. And I think it's the kind of thing that each group can/should workout on its own because a solid answer locks out all alternate stories.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-04T11:29:30-08:00","id":754597,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/751417-are-people-born-solar?p=754574#post754574\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's the thing though: the CHARACTERS don't know how true soul-metaphysics works. So is it something that needs to be laid out in the Core? What is harmed by the whole thing being ambiguous and mysterious?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's true. <br /> <br /> Then again, the CHARACTERS don't know how the empress disappeared. Until they try to find her. The CHARACTERS don't know the source of the abyssal exalted. Until they try to figure it out. <br /> <br /> The CHARACTERS don't know about the great curse yet is a quest to reverse it out of the works now? <br /> <br /> I feel like I'm looking at a wall with a huge hole in it. Someone has plastered &quot;remember when this wasn't a hole&quot; over top of it and whenever I ask &quot;why don't they fix the hole?&quot; or &quot;what's up with this hole&quot; everybody is like &quot;nah bro it's not a hole at all&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-04T11:33:13-08:00","id":754600,"title":"","content":"The disappearance of the Empress is a thing that actually drives character interactions, whether that be in defining how characters in various former satrapies plan their futures, what the immediate concerns of people who might fight over succession may be, or where a character hoping to solve the mystery and possibly avert the crisis might go.<br /> <br /> One Sidereal sends another a report laying down opinions about all the things that might have happened to the Empress, several of which are concerns even if they have nothing to do with her (like, hey, some cagey demon politics going on, might look into that in its own right). Those Sidereals, along with three or four friends, then get together and pursue all of those leads, getting into crazy adventures along the way.<br /> <br /> What do these distinctions you are failing to see around Exaltation (which I'm honestly still not quite sure of, because I find some of these complaints a bit impenetrable) actually contribute to play?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-04T11:38:09-08:00","id":754606,"title":"","content":"I mean... here are basic facts that can be gleaned within the first forty pages:<br /> <br /> * Exaltations are something that can be imprisoned.<br /> * Exaltation is something bestowed upon you by powerful gods.<br /> * Exaltation comes at certain later moments in your life, often when you have this broad set of characteristics.<br /> * Being Exalted means that you have occasional flashes of memory from previous Exalted people.<br /> <br /> What are the glaring gaps?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-04T11:41:21-08:00","id":754611,"title":"","content":"I think the Glossary's definition of &quot;Second Breath&quot; makes the implications pretty clear.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-04T11:48:47-08:00","id":754624,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>armyofwhispers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/751417-are-people-born-solar?p=754597#post754597\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's true. <br /> <br /> Then again, the CHARACTERS don't know how the empress disappeared. Until they try to find her. The CHARACTERS don't know the source of the abyssal exalted. Until they try to figure it out. <br /> <br /> The CHARACTERS don't know about the great curse yet is a quest to reverse it out of the works now? <br /> <br /> I feel like I'm looking at a wall with a huge hole in it. Someone has plastered &amp;quot;remember when this wasn't a hole&amp;quot; over top of it and whenever I ask &amp;quot;why don't they fix the hole?&amp;quot; or &amp;quot;what's up with this hole&amp;quot; everybody is like &amp;quot;nah bro it's not a hole at all&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Note that the book doesn't say what happened to the Empress or the source of the Abyssal Exalted, because those are completely open questions for Solar PCs. The latter will be revealed when the Abyssal book comes out of course, but the former will never be answered because it's intentionally left to the storyteller to define at their table.<br /> <br /> The whole ethos of Third Edition is to recapture the sense of wonder, myth, and mystery from early first edition, before all this stuff was overanalyzed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-04T11:57:18-08:00","id":754639,"title":"","content":"I feel as though the Abyssals book may not even go so far as to give a straightforward origin story for them.<br /> <br /> I mean, the conceit of being an appropriation of Solar Exaltation maybe, but perhaps not an actual thing of &quot;the Yozis found the Jade Prison, broke it open, and scooped up all of the Essences they could get, to bring back for their magic cages&quot;.<br /> <br /> It could be something that maintains the tone established by this corebook, in which the return of the Solars is taken as writ, without an overt explanation. That's something that even the Second Edition core did.<br /> <br /> On that note, I'll point out that this book's depiction of Exaltation is extremely similar to that of the First Edition one, so unless the very first Exalted book was written with an assumption that you needed the knowledge of books that wouldn't come out for years in order to understand it...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-04T12:01:52-08:00","id":754664,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/751417-are-people-born-solar?p=754587#post754587\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What value does a single Word of God answer provide? What does it do except end OOC or IC debate that might happen at tables before it even could start, since someone can point at a book and say &quot;page N says it means X and it works in Y way so you're wrong?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>By this logic you or your players are completely unable to invoke &quot;the orichalcum rule&quot; Isn't that <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/751417-are-people-born-solar?p=754587#post754587\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">your hangup to deal with</div> </div> </div> </div>?<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/751417-are-people-born-solar?p=754587#post754587\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How are the Exaltations more important than the Exalted? What value does answering the question &quot;what is (an) Exaltation&quot; in an OOC context actually provide? How does it actually facilitate gaming in the system or the setting?</div> </div> </div> </div>Never once said they were and I'm honestly unsure why you keep beating up that straw guy over there.<br /> <br /> My point is that despite the players being the most important thing in the setting, the exaltations themselves are still worthy of <i>some</i> word count to explain them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/751417-are-people-born-solar?p=754587#post754587\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The fact that the Empress disappeared is much more important to the setting than a philosophical/physics discussion of &quot;what is an Exaltation.&quot; The Empress had to be gone for the story of the Solars' return to be possible since they can't effectively stand against a unified, powerful Realm.</div> </div> </div> </div>So? Of course it's important to the setting that her rednessis gone. But <b>h</b><b>ow </b>the empress disappeared is <b>not important</b>.<br /> <br /> The exact mechanism of the empresses' disappearance is immaterial compared to the fact that she <b>is </b>gone and left behind a power vacuum. Enter Solars.<br /> <br /> I guess that by your reasoning they wasted an entire half a page laying out possibilities on how she disappeared.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-04T12:04:16-08:00","id":754678,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/751417-are-people-born-solar?p=754624#post754624\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Note that the book doesn't say what happened to the Empress or the source of the Abyssal Exalted, because those are completely open questions for Solar PCs. The latter will be revealed when the Abyssal book comes out of course, but the former will never be answered because it's intentionally left to the storyteller to define at their table.<br /> <br /> The whole ethos of Third Edition is to recapture the sense of wonder, myth, and mystery from early first edition, before all this stuff was overanalyzed.</div> </div> </div> </div>They did lay out possible explanations for her redness though and they foreshadow the crap out of the abyssals. My complaint is that they did not level the same courtesy to the exaltations. <br /> <br /> All I'm looking for is a sidebar basically saying: &quot;hey, no one but the gods know exactly how the exaltations works, but here are some possibilities.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-04T12:13:01-08:00","id":754712,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>armyofwhispers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/751417-are-people-born-solar?p=754678#post754678\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They did lay out possible explanations for her redness though and they foreshadow the crap out of the abyssals. My complaint is that they did not level the same courtesy to the exaltations.<br /> <br /> All I'm looking for is a sidebar basically saying: &quot;hey, no one but the gods know exactly how the exaltations works, but here are some possibilities.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Honest question: does that impact your game, and if so, how?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a Woman, I'm a GM. <i>Of course</i> I'm Evil.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/424-dawaterrat","name":"DaWaterRat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar424_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-04T12:14:14-08:00","id":754727,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>armyofwhispers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/751417-are-people-born-solar?p=754664#post754664\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I guess that by your reasoning they wasted an entire half a page laying out possibilities on how she disappeared.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, if it had taken any form other than in-character speculation that also fills out a bit more of the history of the world and a few active plot hooks (there have been a couple of Lunars operating around the Imperial City, there is some agitation of unknown source among demon factions, the Empress had a tendency to bring Exalted into the Imperial Manse), it absolutely would have been.<br /> <br /> When you make it in-character, you give it an edge of fallibility that means you don't have to commit to a sense of not contradicting any of the open ends that prevents ever bringing the Empress up ever again; if any other book adds a peripheral fact that contradicts any of the possibilities laid out there, it doesn't mean you undermined one of your options, you just had a character who didn't know it all. By attaching each of those possibilities to things that are significant in their own right, you can use it to provide insights into the setting that somebody can pick up on even if they're never interested in the subject of the Empress.<br /> <br /> What do you get of anywhere near that value by laying out even one mechanistic explanation of precisely where Exaltation ends and you begin, let alone multiple ones?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-04T13:05:03-08:00","id":754827,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DaWaterRat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/751417-are-people-born-solar?p=754712#post754712\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Honest question: does that impact your game, and if so, how?</div> </div> </div> </div>1. Any game that deals directly with the nature of exaltation, yes<br /> <br /> 2. Any game that deals with the great curse, yes... well, not necessarily depending on the curse but that's another question entirely.<br /> <br /> 3. Any game that deals with creating your own exaltations, yes<br /> <br /> 4. Any game that deals with talking directly to TUS, probably not but definitely a possible direction to take.<br /> <br /> 5. Any game where someone tries to sorcerously change the nature of another exalted, or your own exaltation, yes<br /> <br /> These aren't the only ways that it could effect gameplay certainly but off the cuff these come to mind.<br /> <br /> As for <b>how</b> they impact gameplay, are any of these unclear as stated? I can certainly explain my reasoning in depth if you wish me too. Otherwise, see below.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">When you make it in-character, you give it an edge of fallibility that means you don't have to commit to a sense of not contradicting any of the open ends that prevents ever bringing the Empress up ever again; if any other book adds a peripheral fact that contradicts any of the possibilities laid out there, it doesn't mean you undermined one of your options, you just had a character who didn't know it all. By attaching each of those possibilities to things that are significant in their own right, you can use it to provide insights into the setting that somebody can pick up on even if they're never interested in the subject of the Empress.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can certainly agree with your reasoning as to the importance of delivery method, but at the same time you can easily do an in character blurb on the nature of exaltation. Have somebody discover the musings of a first age savant delving in to this very question.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Regardless I've come to a realization: I will almost certainly get what I want in the book dealing with the nature of exaltation and the creation of unique types of exalts: The Exigents.<br /> <br /> I can wait until then to really sink my teeth into these topics. Until then I think we've mostly beaten this topic to death :-P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-04T13:33:53-08:00","id":754864,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>armyofwhispers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/751417-are-people-born-solar?p=754664#post754664\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By this logic you or your players are completely unable to invoke &quot;the orichalcum rule&quot; Isn't that<br /> <br /> Never once said they were and I'm honestly unsure why you keep beating up that straw guy over there.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, you're incorrect as to &quot;my logic.&quot;<br /> <br /> My point is, you are bringing in preconceptions from another edition. The authors said this is a thing you shouldn't do. It's not the book's job to convince you not to bring in those preconceptions. The book is written as if readers are totally unfamiliar with Exalted and have never seen another edition. It shouldn't be in the business of things like, &quot;well if you read 2e, XYZ were different, and here's how we're handling it for 3e.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>armyofwhispers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/751417-are-people-born-solar?p=754664#post754664\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My point is that despite the players being the most important thing in the setting, the exaltations themselves are still worthy of <i>some</i> word count to explain them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I disagree.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>armyofwhispers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/751417-are-people-born-solar?p=754664#post754664\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess that by your reasoning they wasted an entire half a page laying out possibilities on how she disappeared.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope about &quot;my logic,&quot; because the disappearance of Scarlet is actually a meaningful plot the players can pursue and which affects the in-setting world around them, whereas &quot;what is the nature of my Exaltation&quot; generally is not. Though Isator said it better than me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-04T13:50:08-08:00","id":754877,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/751417-are-people-born-solar?p=754864#post754864\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My point is, you are bringing in preconceptions from another edition. The authors said this is a thing you shouldn't do. It's not the book's job to convince you not to bring in those preconceptions. The book is written as if readers are totally unfamiliar with Exalted and have never seen another edition. It shouldn't be in the business of things like, &quot;well if you read 2e, XYZ were different, and here's how we're handling it for 3e.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, I'm gonna try one more time to clear this up. First:<br /> <br /> What preconceptions do I hold from 2nd edition? <br /> <br /> If you can answer that maybe I'll have a chance at addressing your concerns. <br /> <br /> As to the second part there, we are in PERFECT AGREEMENT. No one should EVER have to read a previous edition to figure out the setting in the new edition. That's a huge part of the whole point of this thread, but it seems to have been imperfectly communicated. <br /> <br /> So I ask again: What preconceptions are you talking about? Precisely.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-04T15:13:11-08:00","id":755015,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>armyofwhispers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/751417-are-people-born-solar?p=754877#post754877\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What preconceptions do I hold from 2nd edition?</div> </div> </div> </div>You seem to be* arguing that because 3e is deliberately not going into great detail about the nature of the Exaltations and their in-setting mechanics (as 2e did, at length), that the setting does not make sense or that there's a plot hole.<br /> <br /> You seem to be arguing that the 3e authors should be presenting the nature of the Exaltations in an objective, factual, unequivocal way, like 2e did, or at the very least giving a set of options for how the Exaltations should be presented.<br /> <br /> You seem to be saying that 3e may be Doing It Wrong because it's not going into exhaustive detail about the Exaltations, like 2e did.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> *of course, these are totally based on my perception, and you might read this and say, &quot;I really don't think I'm doing that!&quot; So I'm not trying to say you <i>objectively are doing this</i>, just, from <i>my subjective perspective</i>, this is what is coming across to me and where my responses are coming from.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>armyofwhispers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/751417-are-people-born-solar?p=754551#post754551\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm talking about how exaltion in 3E is written as if things that were true in 2E are still true. Except they aren't explained in 3E. I think we can all agree that exaltation is pretty pivotal to the setting.<br /> <br /> It's more like the writers require us to carry all the baggage through from 2E. Otherwise it doesn't make a whole lot of sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is maybe where I started thinking you were carrying something forward. I'm not seeing how Exaltation in 3e is written as if things that were 2e are still true. And I'm not sure that a clearly-delineated process of Exaltation is actually needed for the setting to make sense (as was said, it really wasn't explained in 1e, and people didn't give a ton of shit then, which makes it seem* like because 2e went into great detail, that 3e is morally obligated somehow to go into great detail or something, because detail was given at some point and retracting detail going forward is bad for some reason? I'm not sure)<br /> <br /> *as above<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>armyofwhispers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/751417-are-people-born-solar?p=754877#post754877\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not saying that an explanation of exaltation is necessary to play Exalted. It's really not. Most often it happens off screen. It's a big part of most pre-game history...</div> </div> </div> </div>See, here I'm not sure if you're referring to a particular character's Exaltation scene, or like...ancient history discussing how the Exaltations were made, etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-04T16:12:45-08:00","id":755174,"title":"","content":"George R. R. Martin didn't give an explicit statement on the objective nature of the red comet in <i>A Clash of Kings</i>? Not even in a sidebar?<br /> <br /> What a hack! ASoIaF ruined <b>forevar</b>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-04T16:28:28-08:00","id":755210,"title":"","content":"Hmmm... <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In the world of Exalted, the soul enters an individual\u2019s body when she draws her first breath. When a being is Exalted, the rush of divine energy is very similar, and Exaltation is, thus, often called the Second Breath. </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Exalted are those humans deemed worthy by the greatest of the spirits to taste the sting of power. Since the truth of the nature of the Exalted has never been made known, at least not since the beginning of the current Age, their precise nature can only be speculated upon. Mystics and madmen ramble on about one superstitious theory or another, but most of them are lying, deluded or, perhaps, something in between. </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The rules of Terrestrial heredity are complex and poorly understood, and the only rule of Celestial Exaltation is that the Exalted individual is already far above average \u2014 always in term of potential, and usually in term of life-accomplishment as well. </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The powers of an Exalted frequently manifest after a period of stress \u2014 severe injury, terrible illness, terror. The trigger events vary greatly from Exalted to Exalted. At his hour of greatest need, it is as if the character is given the strength to triumph and endure. Some Celestials also manifest when they are exposed to a large amount of magic or when a great deal of Essence is moved or channeled near them. </div> </div> </div> This is about the extent of what the First Edition core said about the subject.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-05T08:25:22-08:00","id":756604,"title":"","content":"First off, Zelbinnean thank you for responding to me. I will do my best to clear up my meaning for your benefit and hopefully explain my meaning for others along the way.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/751417-are-people-born-solar?p=755015#post755015\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You seem to be* arguing that because 3e is deliberately not going into great detail about the nature of the Exaltations and their in-setting mechanics (as 2e did, at length), that the setting does not make sense or that there's a plot hole.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not necessarily. To my mind we don't need an actual word of god &quot;This is what exaltation is and that's how we're running it.&quot; Same way we don't need an exact explanation of how her redness went missing. Or how the abyssal exalts were created. Or who the 'enemies of the gods' were that cursed the exalted.<br /> <br /> Except in the case of the abyssal exalted, the enemies of the gods, and I think exaltation itself there is an actual answer that the writers have in mind. The scarlet empress scenario is kinda like exalted mad libs. Choose whatever works best for you and go with it.<br /> <br /> My problem is that they didn't treat these issues the same way. They're written as if there's a one true answer that they hint the crap out of in the case of the abyssal exalted or make absolutely no assumptions about in the case of the enemies of the gods.<br /> <br /> With exaltation they make assumptions about the behavior of the exaltations without effectively (to my mind) hinting at any good one answer. This is the worst when they're talking about past lives or reincarnation. They talk as if it was you in the first age. Not your exaltation, but <i>you.</i> What are new players supposed to interpret that as?<br /> <br /> That's why I titled the thread as I did. Because from the text of 3E the most probable explanation is that someone is somehow born a solar but only gets access to that power later on. What else does talk of reincarnation of solars (not the exaltations as separate things but the solars themselves reincarnating) and talking about <i>your</i> past lives where you were a solar suggest? I don't think the authors were trying to come across that way but...<br /> <br /> If they were going for actual ambiguity then why didn't they treat it the same way as they did for the &quot;enemies of the gods?&quot; Strip out any reference to who the actual enemies were and just use them as a setting piece.<br /> <br /> Here's what I mean: Instead of talking about the usurpation as &quot;<i>Most of the Solars were murdered and their Essences </i><i>sealed away in a jade prison\u2014for such was their power </i><i>that they could reincarnate upon death.&quot;</i> Talk about how &quot;Such was their power that new solars would otherwise endlessly spring forth. Or something along those lines. It shows that there was a need to lock away the solars without actually implying that the new solars are reincarnations of past solars. You can do this with every reference to past life, solars or exaltation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/751417-are-people-born-solar?p=755015#post755015\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You seem to be arguing that the 3e authors should be presenting the nature of the Exaltations in an objective, factual, unequivocal way, like 2e did, or at the very least giving a set of options for how the Exaltations should be presented.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't necessarily think we need a &quot;one true explanation&quot; but I honestly feel that they've written as if there is one true explanation and it comes across like they just forgot to share that with readers. If they really wanted to create pure ambiguity then treat it the same way they treat the 'enemies of the gods.' If they're trying to set it up to be discussed further in another book (IE the exigents), then I feel they should have treated it similar to the abyssals. Make it mysterious and hint at things but don't reveal the mechanism.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/751417-are-people-born-solar?p=755015#post755015\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You seem to be saying that 3e may be Doing It Wrong because it's not going into exhaustive detail about the Exaltations, like 2e did.</div> </div> </div> </div>hmmm. No I don't believe that. I acknowledge I may have come across as thinking that though. I do <i>prefer</i> an explanation to not having one, but it's not a bad thing to have it<br /> <br /> Thing is the writers had several topics that they very specifically weren't going to pin down in the core: The empress, the abyssals, the 'enemies of the gods,' the exaltations etc.<br /> <br /> The empress they give alternate theories (in character so fallible), the abyssals they hint and foreshadow the crap out of as they always have, the enemies of the gods they reference only slightly, but the exaltations they reference all the time, they don't offer even vague or in character explanations. It's like they just didn't care enough to explain why solars got visions of past lives, or why the sidereals had to lock away these 'solar exaltation' things and didn't think that anyone else would wonder why at all.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/751417-are-people-born-solar?p=755015#post755015\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*of course, these are totally based on my perception, and you might read this and say, &quot;I really don't think I'm doing that!&quot; So I'm not trying to say you <i>objectively are doing this</i>, just, from <i>my subjective perspective</i>, this is what is coming across to me and where my responses are coming from.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is why I asked you to explain where you were coming from. Hopefully I've cleared up my position somewhat.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/751417-are-people-born-solar?p=755015#post755015\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is maybe where I started thinking you were carrying something forward. I'm not seeing how Exaltation in 3e is written as if things that were 2e are still true. And I'm not sure that a clearly-delineated process of Exaltation is actually needed for the setting to make sense (as was said, it really wasn't explained in 1e, and people didn't give a ton of shit then, which makes it seem* like because 2e went into great detail, that 3e is morally obligated somehow to go into great detail or something, because detail was given at some point and retracting detail going forward is bad for some reason? I'm not sure)</div> </div> </div> </div>I see that Isator Levi posted what he could find in 1E about exaltations for which I thank him. I've never read 1E, nor have I ever felt I needed to.<br /> <br /> I think the contrast between how it's handled in 3E and 1E is very clear to me now.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <i>Exalted are those humans deemed worthy by the greatest of the spirits to taste the sting of power. Since the truth of the nature of the Exalted has never been made known, at least not since the beginning of the current Age, their precise nature can only be speculated upon. Mystics and madmen ramble on about one superstitious theory or another, but most of them are lying, deluded or, perhaps, something in between.</i> </div> </div> </div>This quote is important.<br /> <br /> This single paragraph is the difference between being <i>deliberately ambiguous</i> with a concept and not thinking the concept is worth any explanation whatsoever and thus leaving it <i>ambiguous by omission</i>.<br /> <br /> This is exactly the word count that I wanted in a sidebar that you said you felt would be wasted earlier in the thread.<br /> <br /> Deliberate ambiguity is fine. Ambiguity by omission is a mistake.<br /> <br /> On another note,<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <i>In the world of Exalted, the soul enters an individual\u2019s body when she draws her first breath. When a being is Exalted, the rush of divine energy is very similar, and Exaltation is, thus, often called the Second Breath.</i> </div> </div> </div>Is actually way <b>less </b>ambiguous than<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Second Breath<br /> The moment of Exaltation, so called because infant mortals gain their souls at the moment of their first breath following birth. </div> </div> </div><br /> Moving on<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/751417-are-people-born-solar?p=755015#post755015\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">See, here I'm not sure if you're referring to a particular character's Exaltation scene, or like...ancient history discussing how the Exaltations were made, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, I'm talking about when you go to play exalted, you determine the circumstances of how your character exalted, but when play starts most groups take it as read that you've been a solar for a while already.<br /> <br /> I meant pre-game history as in - in most exalted games, the actual exaltation of most PCs has already happened. Sorry for not being clear there.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I hope that this clears up my stance as it is. However, I really don't think that there's much point to my complaints any more. I think that there was a mistake made in the handling of the concept of exaltations. I don't want a specific answer to the question &quot;what is an exaltation&quot; but some additional clarity would help, or alternatively the removal or alteration of details relating to the exaltation and past lives could also clear up the issue.<br /> <br /> Regardless, I'm pretty sure they're going to have to go more in depth into the nature of exaltations in the exigent supplement so I think I'll I've said all I want to on this topic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-05T08:34:28-08:00","id":756615,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/751417-are-people-born-solar?p=755174#post755174\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">George R. R. Martin didn't give an explicit statement on the objective nature of the red comet in <i>A Clash of Kings</i>? Not even in a sidebar?<br /> <br /> What a hack! ASoIaF ruined <b>forevar</b>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Trollers gonna troll I guess.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-05T08:34:51-08:00","id":756616,"title":"","content":"The nature of Exigency is not the same as Solar, or Lunar, or Terrestrial, or Liminal Exaltation. It's not even consistent in itself. If you think they will explain it in depth, I have a feeling it's going to be disappointing (for someone, at the very least).<br /> <br /> That said, I don't understand your confusion about Solars being reincarnated. Solars are, indeed, reincarnated. Each Solar, when slain, will eventually be reborn as another person. When you become a Solar Exalt, you are a Solar that came before you, reborn. It doesn't mean you were born as that Solar, but became them upon Exaltation, which you gained through your prowess and peerless will. To think of the Exaltation as a separate thing from your person as a Solar is misleading. It is your identity, as much as what came before you were Exalted, as much as your eyes or your hands, even though, unlike your eyes, you weren't born with it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;From now on, instead of saying 'half-assed', I will use 'muled'. 'This is a muled job, Chris', I will say to my friend Chris. 'You need to do better, or your ass is grass. And not, like, metaphorical grass. There are weeds growing in there as we speak.'<br /> <br /> &quot;'The DEA is after you, man' I will tell him, in all seriousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8891-khantalas","name":"Khantalas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8891_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"899"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-05T08:55:16-08:00","id":756642,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khantalas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/751417-are-people-born-solar?p=756616#post756616\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The nature of Exigency is not the same as Solar, or Lunar, or Terrestrial, or Liminal Exaltation. It's not even consistent in itself. If you think they will explain it in depth, I have a feeling it's going to be disappointing (for someone, at the very least).</div> </div> </div> </div>Nah, I'm not looking for a stat block on an exaltation. <br /> <br /> Any amount of &quot;These are different because x&quot; is still extra definition of both things.The fact that celestial exaltations are different from terrestrial exaltations are differrent from exigent exaltations is exactly what I'm hoping for. <br /> <br /> I'm banking on more than just &quot;they're different because we say they are&quot; out of the writers. they're better than that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}